=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  logforward review-tls ----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Decided: no Figma frame. Set server with hardn.yml asking for$
# TLS: rsyslog-gnutls is installed first, and the file names the$
# driver, the server's name and the CA file.$
$
  Checking the host...$
$
# Set server ###################################################$
$
# Note$
# Every message the host logs goes to the server, as it is$
# logged.$
$
  Forwarding ---------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Server               logs.example.net:6514$
  [+] Protocol             TLS$
   -  CA File              /etc/ssl/lab-ca.pem$
$
   -  Install rsyslog-gnutls$
      rsyslog-gnutls$
      -not installed$
      +installed$
      $ apt-get install -y rsyslog-gnutls$
$
   -  Write hardn's forwarding file$
      /etc/rsyslog.d/60-hardn-forward.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,8 @@$
      +# Written by hardn (Log Forwarding).$
      +*.* action(type="omfwd" protocol="tcp"$
      +    target="logs.example.net" port="6514"$
      +    StreamDriver="gtls" StreamDriverMode="1"$
      +    StreamDriverAuthMode="x509/name"$
      +    StreamDriverPermittedPeers="logs.example.net"$
      +    StreamDriver.CAFile="/etc/ssl/lab-ca.pem"$
      +    queue.type="linkedList")$
      $ rsyslogd -N1$
$
   -  Restart rsyslog$
      rsyslog$
      $ systemctl restart rsyslog$
$
   -  Send a test line$
      $ logger -t hardn "log forwarding set"$
$
  Forward logs to logs.example.net? [y/N, 0 or q]: $
$
$

